      "reading": "This is the first test that SEPARATES the two survivors. Raw scatter left them tied (4.25% vs 4.52%), but their residuals behave differently: H_coth's residuals are essentially structureless (r = -0.33 vs A, lag-1 autocorrelation -0.16), while H_FH_Z's carry a strong systematic trend (r = +0.71, autocorrelation +0.30). A correctly-specified model should leave structureless residuals, so the drift counts AGAINST the Vol^(-1/3) reading and IN FAVOUR of coth-saturation.",
